{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/216345-primium-0","id":216345,"title":"Primium 0","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-01T19:16:50-07:00","id":216345,"title":"Primium 0","content":"In [b]Heirs to Hell[/i], there\u2019s a Merit called Aetheric Pool which gives the Fractal a pool of up to 5 Aether, and the ability to sense Aetheric Resonance. In <b>Blood and Smoke</b>, Ghouls get a Blood Potency 0 trait which gives them a small Blood Pool and a few other limited aspects of what Blood Potency 1+ gives you. What do you think: should Aetheric Pool be thought of as \u201cPrimium 0\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T11:27:36-07:00","id":223421,"title":"","content":"I don't think this would be the best way to think of Aetheric Pool. For one thing, that Ghoul has all the hardware needed to eventually become a Vampire; however, Fractals typically can't become Demons (though the Little Monsters sidebar (DtD p.44) hints at exceptions). <i>Demon: the Descent</i> defines Primum as a measurement of how adapted and integrated the Demon is with reality, instead of the God-Machine. Considering that Fractals are genuine humans and thus fully integrated in reality with no Cover needed, they're in some ways closer to Primum 11 than Primum 0. That's where I think the idea breaks down. <br /> <br /> I think part of what makes hellspawn interesting is that, perhaps more than any of the other lesser templates (Ghouls, Wolf-blooded, Proximi, etc.), they're not really a practice or progressive version of their major template. A Vampire might relate to Ghouls because she shared their state before her Embrace. A Werewolf can feel for his Wolf-blooded niece as tormenting spirits herald her First Change. But the Unchained probably never had a childhood and suspect their children will never be quite the same thing they are. Supernaturally, they share neither a common past, nor a converging future. So I feel like thinking of Aetheric Pool as Primum 0 is assuming similarity when maybe the point is how metaphysically different they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1925-toroid","name":"Toroid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1925_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}